      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MYSTIC SMILE (8) is the horse to beat after justifying favouritism in a Mdn at Ascot, covering ground before scoring by a long neck from Buster's Babe. She had been second at this track over 1000m the start prior and beat TWILIGHT STAR there. Can repeat the dose. MERIVALE LOUVAIN (1) returned with a bang at Bunbury, scoring by 2.1L as a $1.60 pop in a dominant display despite settling near the tail. She'll be better for that effort and she looks a very exciting filly on the way up. Drawing away from the rail is a big bonus and she can get the job done again. TWILIGHT STAR (7) got the job done in this grade last start over 1100m and the slight rise in trip doesn't look an issue. Parnham rides now and another forward showing is expected. CLOBBERCONI (3) was only 1.4L behind TWILIGHT STAR on debut. Better for that effort and can feature again. CRYPTOMANIA (4) gets Pike and the Blinkers on fresh on the back of some nice trials. Not to be discounted.",
